# CodieMind backend — every variable app/config.py reads.
#
# Copy to backend/.env and fill in real values. backend/.env is never committed
# and was never committed (full-history scan, STATUS_2026-09-05.md §2).
#
# Names only below; no values, real or plausible. Every line is commented out,
# so an uncommented copy of this file behaves exactly like no file at all and
# every setting keeps the default in config.py.
#
# pydantic-settings declares no env_prefix, so each variable is the field name
# upper-cased. config.py:14-19 loads backend/.env by absolute path, so these
# apply regardless of the working directory pytest or uvicorn is started from.
#
# 24 variables. The FYP-1 version of this file listed 3 (,
# "Stub — omits OPENAI_API_KEY, LLM_PROVIDER after the swap").

# --- Provider selection --------------------------------------------------
# "openai" (default) or "gemini". Absent from the live .env, which is why the
# system runs gpt-4o-mini despite Gemini-only documentation.
#LLM_PROVIDER=

# --- OpenAI --------------------------------------------------------------
# Secret. Must come from the environment or this file; nothing secret is committed.
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Pinned dated snapshot, never the floating gpt-4o-mini alias.
#OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=
# OpenAI publishes no dated embedding snapshots, so this id is recorded per run
# rather than pinned.
#OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# --- Gemini / Google GenAI -----------------------------------------------
# Secret.
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
# NOT a pinned snapshot: no stable dated id exists for this model, so the Gemini
# path fails REQUIRE_PINNED_CHAT_MODEL and must not serve a benchmark run
# (STATUS_2026-09-05.md §7 item 2).
#GEMINI_CHAT_MODEL=
#GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# --- Decoding -----------------------------------------
# Nothing here may be left to a provider default. OpenAI defaults temperature to
# 1.0, which is why no two repeats of the FYP-1 run were byte-identical.
#LLM_TEMPERATURE=
#LLM_MAX_TOKENS=
# Best-effort on OpenAI; set and recorded so variance is measured, not assumed.
#LLM_SEED=
# When true, refuse to start on a chat model id that is not a dated snapshot.
# Set this for every benchmark run.
#REQUIRE_PINNED_CHAT_MODEL=

# --- Conversation history (Slot 5) ---------------------
# Set HISTORY_ENABLED=false for every benchmark run so Slot 5 is empty and a
# preference cannot reach the prompt except by retrieval.
#HISTORY_ENABLED=
#HISTORY_LIMIT=

# --- Scorer weights ------------------------------------------------------
# Must sum to 1.0. Fixed a priori and documented; DO NOT TUNE. Arm B cannot be
# tuned, so tuning arm C makes the comparison unfair.
#SCORER_RECENCY_WEIGHT=
#SCORER_IMPORTANCE_WEIGHT=
#SCORER_RELEVANCE_WEIGHT=

# --- Context assembler slot budgets (tokens, approx len//4) --------------
#SLOT_USER_QUERY_BUDGET=
#SLOT_PREFERENCES_BUDGET=
#SLOT_DECISIONS_BUDGET=
#SLOT_CODE_CONTEXT_BUDGET=
#SLOT_HISTORY_BUDGET=
#SLOT_REPEATED_QUERY_BUDGET=
# Arm B injects every stored preference at once, so it needs far more room than
# the top-k slot. Over-budget raises rather than truncating, because a truncated
# whole-file baseline is a strawman.
#SLOT_STATIC_PREFERENCES_BUDGET=

# --- Storage -------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime SQLite + ChromaDB root. Defaults to codiemind/.codiemind/.
# Point it at a scratch directory for tests and benchmark runs.
#CODIEMIND_DATA_DIR=
